    {
     "type": "concept",
     "title": "Course Summary: The Ten-Lesson Map",
     "content": "The whole journey on one card. L1 — Classical physics broke on blackbody glow, photoelectric thresholds, and impossible atoms; Planck and Einstein answered with quanta: E = hf. L2 — The double slit revealed wave-particle duality; de Broglie gave everything a wavelength, λ = h/p; which-path knowledge and interference never coexist. L3 — The state ψ holds cancellable amplitudes; the Born rule (P = |amp|², add first, square last) makes probabilities; superposition is genuine; measurement collapses. L4 — Uncertainty, Δx·Δp ≥ ℏ/2, is wave math: it sizes atoms, fuels zero-point jitter, and opens tunnels through walls. L5 — The Schrödinger equation evolves ψ; confined waves quantize; hydrogen's ladder, Eₙ = −13.6/n², decodes every spectral barcode. L6 — Spin's two values plus Pauli's exclusion build shells, the periodic table, solid floors, and white dwarfs. L7 — Entanglement's correlations beat every classical ledger (Bell: 2.83 > 2); local realism died in the lab; signaling never happens. L8 — Interpretations split on what it means: collapse, branches, pilot waves, or betting books — same predictions, different taxes. L9 — The rules became riches: transistors, lasers, MRI, qubits, and physics-guaranteed keys. L10 — You sorted settled from open, demolished the myths, and ran the gauntlet. That is introductory quantum mechanics, complete. Where next, if you're hungry: linear algebra and a first formal course; Feynman's QED for the path-integral view; or the quantum computing track, where Lesson 3's qubits become careers.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"36\" font-weight=\"bold\">The Ten-Lesson Map</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">From crisis to fluency</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"170\" width=\"450\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#6366f1\" opacity=\"0.15\"/><rect x=\"80\" y=\"170\" width=\"450\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"305\" y=\"218\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-size=\"22\" font-weight=\"bold\">L1-2: The break &amp; the wave</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"260\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"19\">E = hf • λ = h/p • double slit</text><rect x=\"570\" y=\"170\" width=\"450\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" opacity=\"0.15\"/><rect x=\"570\" y=\"170\" width=\"450\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"795\" y=\"218\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-size=\"22\" font-weight=\"bold\">L3-4: The state &amp; its limits</text><text x=\"795\" y=\"260\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"19\">Born rule • superposition • ΔxΔp ≥ ℏ/2</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"320\" width=\"450\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#10b981\" opacity=\"0.15\"/><rect x=\"80\" y=\"320\" width=\"450\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"305\" y=\"368\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"22\" font-weight=\"bold\">L5-6: Structure of matter</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"410\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"19\">Schrödinger • levels • spin • Pauli</text><rect x=\"570\" y=\"320\" width=\"450\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#ec4899\" opacity=\"0.15\"/><rect x=\"570\" y=\"320\" width=\"450\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"795\" y=\"368\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-size=\"22\" font-weight=\"bold\">L7-8: Depth &amp; meaning</text><text x=\"795\" y=\"410\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"19\">Bell's verdict • four interpretations</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"470\" width=\"450\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" opacity=\"0.15\"/><rect x=\"80\" y=\"470\" width=\"450\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"305\" y=\"518\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-size=\"22\" font-weight=\"bold\">L9: The payoff</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"560\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"19\">chips • lasers • MRI • qubits • QKD</text><rect x=\"570\" y=\"470\" width=\"450\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#10b981\" opacity=\"0.15\"/><rect x=\"570\" y=\"470\" width=\"450\" height=\"120\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"795\" y=\"518\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"22\" font-weight=\"bold\">L10: The worldview</text><text x=\"795\" y=\"560\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"19\">settled vs. open • myths down</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"630\" width=\"940\" height=\"180\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#ffd700\" opacity=\"0.1\"/><rect x=\"80\" y=\"630\" width=\"940\" height=\"180\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"685\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"26\" font-weight=\"bold\">One-sentence takeaway</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"730\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\">The world runs on cancellable amplitudes; measurement samples them;</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"772\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\">h sets the scale; chemistry and technology are the proof.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"850\" width=\"940\" height=\"170\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#10b981\" opacity=\"0.12\"/><rect x=\"80\" y=\"850\" width=\"940\" height=\"170\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"905\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"26\" font-weight=\"bold\">Where next</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"950\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\">linear algebra + a formal QM course • Feynman's QED •</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"992\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"22\">or the quantum computing track — Lesson 3's qubits become careers</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Ten lessons, five pillars, one worldview — and three roads onward."
     }
    }
